        <body>
            <div xml:id="d706">

                <pb facs="1290" n="1166" sameAs="frus:frus1881/pg1166"/>

                <head>No. 702.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Fish to Mr. Blaine.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Berne</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1881-07-29"><hi rendition="#italic">July</hi> 29, 1881</date>.
                        (Received August 18.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 430.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to my No. 400, concerning the
                    proposed emigration of the widow Olivier and her young children, I have the
                    honor to inclose herewith copies of a further correspondence between the council
                    of Bourgeoisie of Neuveville and this legation.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>NICHOLAS FISH.</signed></closer>




